{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:33.999936Z","id":"5d9fb1b06dbbeb2d292deb3dd7c9b7dfac395105ce317b1c5740571e3aa1aef9","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/mod.rs:536-548, record 4c42016b.\n\nfile_url returns None when not cfg(unix) (url::Url::from_file_path does not exist on wasm32-unknown-unknown), so an export rendered by a hosted build names a project path without its file:// link, where the native daemon gives one. If hosted exports are served, build the URL portably (Url::parse(\"file:///\") and path_segments_mut, matching from_file_path's encoding of SPECIAL_PATH_SEGMENT and its handling of `..`).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":535},"end":{"line":547},"content_hash":"73804433eb012ef149abf1d37d366cf3988131fac12b6a558c31a7c7f396dfca"},"summary":"Off unix, exports render no file:// URL for an absolute path","tags":["wasm","revisit:hosted toolpath exports","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:32:34.250424Z","id":"da8ce607d1c5ff5a0963cc54b24677fa6fad737f4db36d01eb619da1fa77b9a7","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/mod.rs:536-548, record 4c42016b.\n\nfile_url returns None when not cfg(unix) (url::Url::from_file_path does not exist on wasm32-unknown-unknown), so an export rendered by a hosted build names a project path without its file:// link, where the native daemon gives one. If hosted exports are served, build the URL portably (Url::parse(\"file:///\") and path_segments_mut, matching from_file_path's encoding of SPECIAL_PATH_SEGMENT and its handling of `..`).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":551},"end":{"line":563},"content_hash":"73804433eb012ef149abf1d37d366cf3988131fac12b6a558c31a7c7f396dfca"},"summary":"Off unix, exports render no file:// URL for an absolute path","supersedes":"5d9fb1b06dbbeb2d292deb3dd7c9b7dfac395105ce317b1c5740571e3aa1aef9","tags":["wasm","revisit:hosted toolpath exports","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/redact.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:19:16.838434Z","id":"aec9b85f0f5cdf7d6c889928c525d4290a2a744cebce8b78bbea140c2cf05bf3","body":{"detail":"Commit 652f225fcffa (version restore audit fields) also added `\"db_read_grants\"` to fields_class as Class::Safe. At that commit no code writes a db_read_grants field into an artifact.update record: the field belongs to the cross-app read grant work (migration 24, crates/clax-core/src/store/grants.rs), still uncommitted when 652f225fcffa landed. Whether grant contents (artifact IDs of granted readers) are Safe under every redaction option is a decision for that work, and toolpath/tests.rs (the export test around line 1600 that asserts no unclassified fields) does not exercise it. Whoever lands the grant store should test this classification with a recorded grant change, or move the line into that commit's scope.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":313},"end":{"line":313},"content_hash":"655c2658889e9a0dcd807bc7f24dc2468211c3b80066f0d33453185f050cd26e"},"summary":"db_read_grants is classified Safe in artifact.update fields with no code that emits it and no test in the commit that added it","tags":["redaction","review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/tests.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:19:16.838627Z","id":"6ee14b0ee7dd0b75ab9e86e44bc4d701eeba6d73439da23eea6c586bdd93abcc","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/redact.rs:225 classifies version.publish `restored_from` as Safe, which is right for a version number. The test that walks every recorded audit row and asserts redact::unclassified is empty (crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/tests.rs, around line 1620) builds its history without Store::restore_version, and the restore tests in crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs check the stored body, not its redaction. Adding a restore to that fixture would pin the class.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1590},"end":{"line":1625},"content_hash":"f4df98f81f2f3085daeb071c708e2b3ccf96a632b353ab3a48471dcb75ea8503"},"summary":"The every-kind export test records no restore, so nothing fails if restored_from loses its redaction class","tags":["tests","review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/redact.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:25:37.013567Z","id":"94030b06f4e221c812031e71c59b32d7f369e435494c4ba9f2aa54f94fd6511a","body":{"detail":"grant_record writes artifact.update with fields.db_read_grants = {\"grant\"|\"revoke\": <source artifact ID>} and artifact2_id = source. An artifact ID is Safe under every Redaction option (no_text, no_names, no_paths), so the class is right. What is missing is a recorded grant and revoke in the fixture of the every-kind export test (crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/tests.rs around 1590-1625), so a renamed field or a lost class fails a test.","kind":"comment","references":"aec9b85f0f5cdf7d6c889928c525d4290a2a744cebce8b78bbea140c2cf05bf3","summary":"The emitter now exists (crates/clax-core/src/store/grants.rs:40-50, commit 652f225fcffa); the classification is still untested by the export test","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/tests.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:25:37.013584Z","id":"45e02a810539886d9cc4a3f399b33dff295671e5be0ea867efbb85d4a7d5976f","body":{"detail":"The same fixture gap leaves fields.db_read_grants (record aec9b85f) unexercised. One change covers both: call Store::restore_version and Store::grant_read / Store::revoke_read in the fixture before the audit rows are read, so redact::unclassified and assert_valid see version.publish restored_from and artifact.update fields.db_read_grants.","kind":"comment","references":"6ee14b0ee7dd0b75ab9e86e44bc4d701eeba6d73439da23eea6c586bdd93abcc","summary":"Add the restore and a grant/revoke to this fixture together","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/redact.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:28:37.695598Z","id":"32e684a2b941bad45bfb6586dab03662b5d5c7008e7f6ba52553f34c69d8aa57","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"every_recorded_kind_is_classified_and_renders_conformant (crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/tests.rs) now records a grant and a revoke, which emit fields.db_read_grants. Evidence: with db_read_grants removed from fields_class the test fails with `artifact.update: unclassified [\"fields/db_read_grants\"]`; restored, it passes.","supersedes":"aec9b85f0f5cdf7d6c889928c525d4290a2a744cebce8b78bbea140c2cf05bf3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/tests.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:28:37.695752Z","id":"6c57e463682f7fe5521e81552b0694599c2971a9805eeb57658f8513ce51b27a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"The every-kind export fixture now publishes a second version and restores version 1 (restored_from), and makes and revokes a read grant, asserting both are among the live events. Evidence: with restored_from removed from body_class the test fails with `version.publish: unclassified [\"restored_from\"]`; restored, it passes.","supersedes":"6ee14b0ee7dd0b75ab9e86e44bc4d701eeba6d73439da23eea6c586bdd93abcc","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:09.453608Z","id":"0b26a9422446d0ab54ada48b8c5541cad721dd2b8592f5930c6722558d249750","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/mod.rs:536-548, record 4c42016b.\n\nfile_url returns None when not cfg(unix) (url::Url::from_file_path does not exist on wasm32-unknown-unknown), so an export rendered by a hosted build names a project path without its file:// link, where the native daemon gives one. If hosted exports are served, build the URL portably (Url::parse(\"file:///\") and path_segments_mut, matching from_file_path's encoding of SPECIAL_PATH_SEGMENT and its handling of `..`).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":552},"end":{"line":564},"content_hash":"73804433eb012ef149abf1d37d366cf3988131fac12b6a558c31a7c7f396dfca"},"summary":"Off unix, exports render no file:// URL for an absolute path","supersedes":"da8ce607d1c5ff5a0963cc54b24677fa6fad737f4db36d01eb619da1fa77b9a7","tags":["wasm","revisit:hosted toolpath exports","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T02:05:01.054539Z","id":"55f20189d70df60b6ed906b94689c60d942cb5b94ebe71f3f382db41d8eb64da","body":{"detail":"actor_string renders human:clax-reporter/<queue ID>.<reporter ID> and actor_def's identity id is <install>/<queue>/<reporter ID> in every redaction; only `name` is dropped under --no-names. A deployer that uses e-mail addresses as reporter IDs exports them. The spec calls reporter IDs opaque.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":345},"end":{"line":357},"content_hash":"cb808b070dc5ff9b580df6d6c1df69c2a5efd4a4db1175dca59200f173133e36"},"suggested_fix":"Under --no-names, replace the reporter ID with redact::redaction_hash of it in both places.","summary":"A reporter's actor keeps its reporter ID under --no-names: in the actor string and the clax-reporter identity","tags":["session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T05:04:20.900305Z","id":"5a31c301ffa4a51577f7c47dd9bd6dc8a339b10c2f2f2ac5d3ba9211bddbf50c","body":{"detail":"AuditKind gained QueueFix, QueueVerify and QueueReopen (crates/clax-core/src/audit/mod.rs). describe here and field_class in crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/redact.rs (near line 390) name only queue.create/update/claim/release, so a journal record of the new kinds would render with the default description and every body field Unclassified. Nothing records them until the store writes fixes and verdicts (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-29-feedback-loop.md, Task 3), which should add both.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1573},"end":{"line":1573},"content_hash":"32444c06220ee4d8fff8ea3aa9359c2c3a3e9e7bf17e3e2a6b7c6ac0dfc20559"},"summary":"queue.fix, queue.verify and queue.reopen have no description or field classification in the Toolpath rendering yet","tags":["feedback-loop","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T05:04:55.087288Z","id":"4c34faa1927bc39cf2da029e9c55e18ba94d46e4609c379cf59f928d48b8f304","body":{"detail":"AuditKind gained QueueFix, QueueVerify and QueueReopen (crates/clax-core/src/audit/mod.rs), and describe here names them, but field_class in crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/redact.rs (near line 390) classifies body fields only for queue.create/update/claim/release, so every body field of the new kinds is Unclassified. Nothing writes these kinds until the store records fixes and verdicts (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-29-feedback-loop.md, Task 3: queue.fix {thread_id, n, url, commit}), which should classify them: thread_id and n Safe, url Path, commit Safe.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1573},"end":{"line":1586},"content_hash":"e3d63c1de5f3b17498c96993515639a4ea198aec9c0e21a1c252556cedc0c810"},"summary":"queue.fix, queue.verify and queue.reopen bodies have no field classification for redaction yet","supersedes":"5a31c301ffa4a51577f7c47dd9bd6dc8a339b10c2f2f2ac5d3ba9211bddbf50c","tags":["feedback-loop","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T05:17:23.275498Z","id":"4f0926a949e32fa8c5dca0a3e08ad07ca69dea1e2dedf1a2ab4b730151959c09","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:62cadcbae","summary":"Fixed: field_class in crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/redact.rs classifies queue.fix/verify/reopen (url Path; queue_id, thread_id, n, commit, reopen_count, reason Safe) and the golden history holds a row of each; bazel test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test passes, including every_recorded_kind_is_classified_and_renders_conformant.","supersedes":"4c34faa1927bc39cf2da029e9c55e18ba94d46e4609c379cf59f928d48b8f304","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:27.603035Z","id":"098dcf3d92f78b8e6818d3a56253613b6c0722b2ecff636de2396520767b42f2","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/toolpath/mod.rs:536-548, record 4c42016b.\n\nfile_url returns None when not cfg(unix) (url::Url::from_file_path does not exist on wasm32-unknown-unknown), so an export rendered by a hosted build names a project path without its file:// link, where the native daemon gives one. If hosted exports are served, build the URL portably (Url::parse(\"file:///\") and path_segments_mut, matching from_file_path's encoding of SPECIAL_PATH_SEGMENT and its handling of `..`).\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":587},"end":{"line":599},"content_hash":"73804433eb012ef149abf1d37d366cf3988131fac12b6a558c31a7c7f396dfca"},"summary":"Off unix, exports render no file:// URL for an absolute path","supersedes":"0b26a9422446d0ab54ada48b8c5541cad721dd2b8592f5930c6722558d249750","tags":["wasm","revisit:hosted toolpath exports","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/redact.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:22:34.455500Z","id":"26ea61ec9a6fb5dd907348c6fdc576af793c026fd165427f639ebf9441557bec","body":{"detail":"Fields: run, step, op (browser.test or browser.browse), version (absent for the draft), path (the artifact page loaded), url (browse only; Text under --no-text), viewport (a preset's name or <w>x<h>), ms, passed, session (Browser Run's session ID when known), credits_milli, ok and code (a refusal). The golden history row crates/clax-core/tests/toolpath/history.json seq 129 and the description in crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs (Some(K::BotBrowser)) read them. A field the writer adds outside this list falls to the redaction's default class; add it here and to the history row.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":370},"end":{"line":380},"content_hash":"70efc5d338a749826b6aafbe294d4dbd73c3fa4e408b6ee7320587e403277b1b"},"summary":"bot.browser's body fields are fixed here before anything writes the record: the Spend path (plan docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser.md Task 9) must write these names","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:54:47.733156Z","id":"2b436ff83080c1c7ee8434e297c2b9ce11e851a8113e530341a17a6635c0f938","body":{"detail":"The bot.browser description calls every record with ok false 'was refused <op> (<code>)'. That wording comes from bot.web, where a failure is almost always a refusal. For the browser, a browser_timeout, a browser_unavailable after the open, or a cancelled test also has ok false, yet it ran and was charged (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs:565-612). An exported trail then reads, for example, 'ClaxBot run r1 was refused browser.test (browser_timeout) (step 2, 0.02 credits)': a refusal with a charge.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1476},"end":{"line":1477},"content_hash":"ba5b93ba6db4af71cf6409f24d672b12a6780d069e93748bf68affda373b9067"},"suggested_fix":"Describe ok false with credits_milli > 0 (or `ms` present) as a test that ran and failed, for example 'tested the draft (index.html) at desktop: browser_timeout'. Keep 'was refused' for records with no `ms`, and add a row of each to crates/clax-core/tests/toolpath/history.json.","summary":"A browser test charged for a failure after its browser opened is described in exports as 'was refused'","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:57:02.512417Z","id":"8d6f464f4dc545aeefb35bc91778abf84369da7aad9dd845a2bff55def811699","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs:1476-1477: `_ if self.body.get(\"ok\") == Some(&Value::Bool(false)) => format!(\"was refused {} ({})\", op, code)` with no distinction by ms or credits_milli, followed by '(step N, X credits)'. crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs:602-611: a run_test Err after the open (browser_timeout, browser_unavailable after open, cancelled) finishes with res Err, usage Some and counted true, so its record has ok false and a nonzero charge. Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md section 5.4 (lines 425-426) and 8.2 (lines 574-578) say these are charged. Suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"2b436ff83080c1c7ee8434e297c2b9ce11e851a8113e530341a17a6635c0f938","summary":"confirmed: every bot.browser record with ok false is described 'was refused', including charged failures after the open","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/redact.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T17:15:05.091759Z","id":"8f60581c62afcd39280553203564defe017e6814c3d8ae72e2d9ac1211d98d94","body":{"detail":"Classified Safe: capability, run, step, op, ok, code, credits_milli, provider, source, format, request_id, stored, session, kind (a session's source kind), viewport, version, path, ms, passed, reason (a host end's: idle, lifetime, revoked, credits, run_ended). Text: query, url. The golden history row crates/clax-core/tests/toolpath/history.json seq 131 (a browser.session.end) and the description in crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs (Some(K::BotSpend)) read them. A field the writer adds outside this list falls to the redaction's default class; add it here and to the history row.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":382},"end":{"line":393},"content_hash":"10d344add1566cc957f7212054897799cfed909b71f1352617403ab1ae13c098"},"summary":"bot.spend's body fields are fixed here before anything writes the record: the one Spend path (plan docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-unify.md Task 6) must write these names","tags":["claxbot-unify","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T19:06:57.474980Z","id":"732ff3988637f335d89096bb330b69d9b58f7f49431b581edc5b4dd9ed705fe4","body":{"kind":"comment","ref":"git:91de6f4a7","references":"2b436ff83080c1c7ee8434e297c2b9ce11e851a8113e530341a17a6635c0f938","summary":"Still open, and wider since commit 91de6f4a7: every browser call is now a bot.spend record, so the bot.spend arm's 'was refused <op> (<code>)' for ok false (crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs, K::BotSpend) also names a charged browser_timeout or cancelled test a refusal. A record with ok false and credits_milli > 0 ran and was charged.","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T01:32:29.533241Z","id":"8121c5b34c89836cfffd2e3fa8b70d27c35b7fd78fdfadc2910ed125ceab11fe","body":{"detail":"The bot.browser description calls every record with ok false 'was refused <op> (<code>)'. That wording comes from bot.web, where a failure is almost always a refusal. For the browser, a browser_timeout, a browser_unavailable after the open, or a cancelled test also has ok false, yet it ran and was charged (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs:565-612). An exported trail then reads, for example, 'ClaxBot run r1 was refused browser.test (browser_timeout) (step 2, 0.02 credits)': a refusal with a charge.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1473},"end":{"line":1474},"content_hash":"1a97df52dbb746d99f1ed5895d5e186358f2743f2d1e54d7af8d1dcd1fb87d80"},"suggested_fix":"Describe ok false with credits_milli > 0 (or `ms` present) as a test that ran and failed, for example 'tested the draft (index.html) at desktop: browser_timeout'. Keep 'was refused' for records with no `ms`, and add a row of each to crates/clax-core/tests/toolpath/history.json.","summary":"A browser test charged for a failure after its browser opened is described in exports as 'was refused'","supersedes":"2b436ff83080c1c7ee8434e297c2b9ce11e851a8113e530341a17a6635c0f938","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/redact.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T01:32:31.463693Z","id":"c29e6c2794bec64a688f85ed3547366459a66de4f0c2bbcc1105b3f70a18b9aa","body":{"detail":"Classified Safe: capability, run, step, op, ok, code, credits_milli, provider, source, format, request_id, stored, session, kind (a session's source kind), viewport, version, path, ms, passed, reason (a host end's: idle, lifetime, revoked, credits, run_ended). Text: query, url. The golden history row crates/clax-core/tests/toolpath/history.json seq 131 (a browser.session.end) and the description in crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs (Some(K::BotSpend)) read them. A field the writer adds outside this list falls to the redaction's default class; add it here and to the history row.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":370},"end":{"line":381},"content_hash":"3de9a432b4028b8cbbf7bb135cfd88d51d74773f0c36885de68341426750a040"},"summary":"bot.spend's body fields are fixed here before anything writes the record: the one Spend path (plan docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-unify.md Task 6) must write these names","supersedes":"8f60581c62afcd39280553203564defe017e6814c3d8ae72e2d9ac1211d98d94","tags":["claxbot-unify","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/redact.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T01:32:34.710135Z","id":"297317cf938604da94b518fd56d86258867d75722a5c77d201f439294f882295","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Obsolete: 18f91465d removed the bot.browser audit kind (crates/clax-core/src/audit/mod.rs) and its redaction rows; nothing ever wrote it outside this branch, and bot.spend's rows (crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/redact.rs, record 8f60581c) cover browser calls.","supersedes":"26ea61ec9a6fb5dd907348c6fdc576af793c026fd165427f639ebf9441557bec","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T09:52:26.392220Z","id":"35a90329a85df45274cbd7121237450d5b9e64f4e5f457a16f714ed7362448ee","body":{"detail":"The bot.browser description calls every record with ok false 'was refused <op> (<code>)'. That wording comes from bot.web, where a failure is almost always a refusal. For the browser, a browser_timeout, a browser_unavailable after the open, or a cancelled test also has ok false, yet it ran and was charged (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs:565-612). An exported trail then reads, for example, 'ClaxBot run r1 was refused browser.test (browser_timeout) (step 2, 0.02 credits)': a refusal with a charge.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1488},"end":{"line":1489},"content_hash":"1a97df52dbb746d99f1ed5895d5e186358f2743f2d1e54d7af8d1dcd1fb87d80"},"suggested_fix":"Describe ok false with credits_milli > 0 (or `ms` present) as a test that ran and failed, for example 'tested the draft (index.html) at desktop: browser_timeout'. Keep 'was refused' for records with no `ms`, and add a row of each to crates/clax-core/tests/toolpath/history.json.","summary":"A browser test charged for a failure after its browser opened is described in exports as 'was refused'","supersedes":"8121c5b34c89836cfffd2e3fa8b70d27c35b7fd78fdfadc2910ed125ceab11fe","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
